OL,3,GNEWSAWhy is a replica Spanish galleon
OL,4,Ain the west of Scotland?
OL,5,
OL,6,FThe waters at Ayr harbour commonly host
OL,7,Fcommercial cargo ships and visits from
OL,8,Fthe Waverley paddle steamer.
OL,10,FHowever for the past two weeks a very
OL,11,Fdifferent sort of vessel has been
OL,12,Fberthed there - a replica of a 17th
OL,13,FCentury Spanish galleon, complete with
OL,14,Fnational flag fluttering in the breeze.
OL,16,FThe tall ship Galeon Andalucia,
OL,17,Fdescribed as a floating museum by crew
OL,18,Fmembers, will depart Ayrshire on
OL,19,FMonday, heading off to Tobermory on the
OL,20,FIsle of Mull as its tour around Europe
OL,21,Fcontinues.
OL,23,APub: 21-AugQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB  Scot NewsC Reg TVF  Weather
